  "id": "COMPOUND:30682 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside appears to interact with Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through a series of molecular pathways. The compound is directly linked to SNU-387, which is a target of multiple entities, including Dendocarbin K and a complex compound with a specific structure. This suggests that Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside may act as a modulator of signaling pathways involving SNU-387, which in turn targets Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. The evidence points to a potential role in the activation or regulation of this kinase, possibly through the modulation of downstream signaling cascades. The integration of multiple targets and their relationships highlights a possible mechanism where Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside influences the activity of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
